 "text": "Two years ago, I sold my car and bought a bicycle. Many friends thought I had made a mistake. The ride to work takes about twenty minutes, and the road is mostly level. In the first week, my legs were tired, and I arrived a little late. After a month, the ride felt easy. I now save money on fuel and parking. I also get exercise without visiting a gym. On rainy days, I wear a light jacket and leave a little earlier. The bicycle is not right for everyone. But if your trip is short, it is worth a try. You may even start to look forward to the ride."
